CKEditor 5 — NOT bundled in this repository, fetched at install time
  https://github.com/ckeditor/ckeditor5
  Copyright (c) 2003-2026 CKSource Holding sp. z o.o.
  Dual-licensed: GNU General Public License Version 2 or later, OR commercial
  terms from CKSource.

  `npm run fetch-editor` downloads CKEditor into admin/ui/ and configures it
  with licenseKey "GPL". Those files are gitignored: an Apache-2.0 repository
  should not ship a GPL binary, and an installer should meet that choice
  knowingly rather than inherit it.

  Consequence worth understanding before you distribute a build: the admin
  console as deployed combines Apache-2.0 code with GPL code, and the GPL's
  terms govern that combination. If that does not suit your situation, the
  options are a commercial licence from CKSource or a permissively-licensed
  editor. The coupling is deliberately small — create, getData, setData, one
  change event and one image insertion — so substituting one is hours of work.

  This is a description of the licences involved, not legal advice.

DB-IP City Lite database — NOT bundled, fetched by infra/fetch-geodb.mjs
  https://db-ip.com
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
  Attribution is displayed in the console's Stats tab, which is what CC BY
  requires of anyone who uses it.

Google Identity Services — loaded from accounts.google.com at runtime
  https://developers.google.com/identity/gsi/web
  Required for "Sign in with Google"; the token has to be minted by Google in
  the browser. This is the one third-party script the console executes.
